# FUTURE — nice-to-have follow-ups (chat)

- Chat-focused document viewing is outside the readable project-route cutover.
  When it is designed, give it its own project/Work authority and route contract;
  do not reuse the Editor's retained-document controller implicitly.

- ThreadSwitcherPopover recomputes filtering/grouping (`filterThreadsByTitle`,
  work-item regrouping) on every render even while the popover is closed.
  Harmless at today's thread counts; if long-task violations appear during
  streaming with many threads, gate the derivation on `open` or memoize it.
  (Noted during slice-7 round-4 review, 2026-07-15.)

- Expanded-fold rail polish, three items observed in the chat-surface rail
  probe (2026-07-24), all cosmetic and deliberately left as-is:
  - A 6px orphan rail tick below a fold whose last row is a tool row.
    Inherent to the self-contained rail (every tool row paints the stub that
    keeps the rail continuous); suppressing it on the last row needs the
    sibling-aware CSS `ActivityRow` already tried and abandoned.
  - Rail rhythm alternates 3px vs 7px gaps at run boundaries, from
    `space-y-1` on the run wrapper.
  - The icon chip fill (`bg-chip-muted-bg`) sits ~2% from the fold
    background, so only the glyph reads and the rail's 26px interruption is
    bridged by an icon rather than a solid chip. Token decision.

- `partitionTurn` walks the whole block list every render. Items are already
  keyed by identity (`itemRenderKey`), so an incremental walk could reuse
  unchanged items per frame instead of re-walking the turn. Not needed at
  current sizes; revisit if streaming with many long turns shows partition
  cost. (Noted during the #558 render-model work, 2026-09-18.)

- Streamdown wraps a markdown image in a `<div>`, which lands inside the
  paragraph `<p>` and logs a React hydration warning (`<div>` cannot be a
  descendant of `<p>`). Upstream streamdown rendering, pre-existing; revisit
  on a streamdown upgrade rather than patching the wrapper here.
  (Noted during the #558 image probe, 2026-09-18.)

- A user-attached image does not render in the user turn: `UserTurn` skips
  non-text blocks, so the transcript shows a link, not the picture. Pre-existing
  composer/UserTurn gap, outside the #558 render model.
  (Noted during the #558 image probe, 2026-09-18.)
